<title>USA: John H. Harland Q2 June 30 profit vs loss.</title>
<headline>John H. Harland Q2 June 30 profit vs loss.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months</p>
<p>					 June 30, 1997    June 30, 1996</p>
<p> Net Sales			    $   139,691   $   149,645</p>
<p>Income (Loss) Before</p>
<p>   Income Taxes			    11,268	(79,251)</p>
<p> Provision for Income Taxes	     4,676	(28,188)</p>
<p> Net Income (Loss)			  6,592	(51,063) (B)</p>
<p> Net Income (Loss) per Common Share     .21	  (1.66) (B)</p>
<p>Average Number of Shares Outstanding</p>
<p>						 30,997	  30,862</p>
<p>							Six Months</p>
<p>					   Jun 30, 1997    Jun 30, 1996</p>
<p> Net Sales				$   278,957     $   301,892</p>
<p>Income (Loss) Before</p>
<p>   Income Taxes				19,854	  (64,838)</p>
<p> Provision for Income Taxes		 8,239	  (22,221)</p>
<p> Net Income (Loss)		     11,615 (A)	  (42,617)</p>
<p> Net Income (Loss) per Common Share   .37 (A)	    (1.38)</p>
<p> Average Number of Shares Outstanding  31,126	    30,709</p>
<p>(A)  Includes $1.6 million, after tax, or $0.05 per share for the six-month period relating to restructuring charges.</p>
<p>(B)  Includes $63.5 million, after tax, or $2.06 per share for the three-month period relating to restructuring charges and expensing of in-process research and development costs resulting from an acquisition.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
</text>
